1.How to you handle logging in your spring boot applications ?
      How to Use SLF4J:
      ----------------
      ->Add Dependency (if not included by default): If you are using Spring Boot, SLF4J and Logback are included by default. Otherwise, you can add the following dependency manually:
          <dependency>
              <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
              <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
              <version>1.7.30</version>
          </dependency>

      ->Declare a Logger object in your class:
             private static final Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(MyClass.class);
      ->Use the logger for different levels of logging:
             logger.info("Application started successfully.");
      ->trace: Fine-grained informational events for debugging.
      ->debug: Detailed information for debugging.
      ->info: General application flow or state.
      ->warn: Potential problems or unexpected behavior.
      ->error: Critical issues or failures.
